    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots the new tenure factor into exactly the unit that already owns this logic. `AssignOwnerMembershipLevel.service` was already a running tally of `level++` factors (email, then namesakeCount), and tenure is added as a third factor in the same shape \u2014 consistent and readable, not bolted on.\n\n- `tenureDays(...)` is extracted as a small private helper rather than inlined, keeping `service` flat and the null/negative handling out of the main flow. Its Javadoc states the contract cleanly. Good altitude.\n- `TENURE_THRESHOLD_DAYS` is a named constant (package-private, matching how tests in this layer typically reach for such values) and is referenced via `{@value}` in the Javadoc, so the doc and code can't drift.\n- Dropping the `Math.min(level, 3)` cap in favor of `setMembershipLevel(level)` is coherent: the max is now exactly 1 + 3 factors = 4, so the cap is no longer needed and leaving it would be misleading.\n- The class stays single-purpose (membership level assignment); nothing turns into a catch-all, and nothing is duplicated.\n- The class Javadoc and the OpenAPI `membershipLevel` schema (range, description) are both updated to match the new behavior, so the edges stay in sync.\n\nLogic is in the right place, idiomatic for the surrounding code, and additive \u2014 a maintainer here would find it natural.",
